From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Gmeiner <cgmeiner@igalia.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 21:18:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 26/57] panfrost: Let a shader jump to another shader when it
 ends

A prolog runs in front of an existing shader. Copying both binaries
into one breaks the PC-relative inline constant pool, so let the
backends end the shader with an absolute jump to the next shader
instead. The target address comes from a FAU word, so the same prolog
binary works in front of any shader. Each shader keeps its own pool.

Helper invocations stay alive, as the next shader may need them for
derivatives.

Signed-off-by: Christian Gmeiner <cgmeiner@igalia.com>
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/40343>
